==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|surcengle||lang=fro}}, formed with {{term|sur||lang=fr|over}} and {{term|cengle||lang=fro|girdle}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈsɜːsɪŋɡ(ə)l/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈsəɹsɪŋɡɫ̩/|lang=en}}
{{rfap|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# a long unpadded strap to pass over and keep in place a blanket, pack or [[saddle]] on an animal
#*{{quote-book|year=1929|author=Baldwyn Dyke Acland|title=Filibuster|chapter=8|edition=|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL219110W|passage=He was standing on the offside of his horse, holding up the flap of his saddle, with the '''surcingle''' loosened, and was pointing to the [[girth#Noun|girths]].  Close to their attachment to the saddle they had been almost cut through with a knife.}}
# a piece of [[tack]] wrapped around the belly of a horse, to use when [[lunge|longeing]], also know as [[lungeing]]; (roller in UK and Australasia)
# a girdle to fasten a garment, especially a cassock

